"sell",more:"More info",adj:"Adjust",x_bias:"Bias",bullish:"Long",bearish:"Short",neutral:"Neutral",x_levels:"Key levels",x_levels_ph:"e.g. PDH 21,290 · London high 21,250",x_plan:"Expected scenario",x_plan_ph:"e.g. A break of the London high that holds on the retest: I buy toward the PDH.",x_alt:"Alternative scenario",x_alt_ph:"e.g. Back under the London low: I sell toward the PDL. Otherwise, no trade.",x_need:"Pick your bias and your max loss.",tip_inst:"The contract you trade today. Micros (MNQ, MES…) are worth 10 times less than minis (NQ, ES…): good to start. E.g. you trade the Nasdaq in micro → MNQ.",tip_london:"The London session runs from about 3:00 to 8:00, New York time. Its high (London high) and its low (London low) are levels where price often reacts at the New York open. E.g. high 21,250, low 21,180. Read them on your chart (just above).",tip_prev:"PDH (previous day high) and PDL (previous day low): the high and the low of yesterday’s session. They are often a target or an obstacle. E.g. PDH 21,290, PDL 21,120. They help propose your targets.",tip_price:"The price when you make your plan. It only pre-selects where the price is on the next screen. You can leave it empty.",tip_a1:"In between: price stayed inside the London session, you wait for it to break out. Above the high or below the low: it already broke out, you play the follow-through or the return.",tip_a2:"The level you watch first makes your main scenario; the other one becomes your alternative scenario. E.g. a Long bias → the London high.",tip_a3:"Yes: price already broke with a 15-min close, your main scenario follows the break. No: it can come back into the London session, your main scenario plays that return. E.g. a 15-min candle closes at 21,262 above a 21,250 high → Yes.",tip_a4:"A level from yesterday right next to your main level. Target: you aim for it. Obstacle: your target stops just before it, as price may stall there. Ignore: it does not count.",tip_news:"High-impact news (CPI, NFP jobs, the Fed’s FOMC) can move price by dozens of points in a minute. Sweep blocks trades from 5 min before to 15 min after. E.g. CPI at 8:30 → no trade from 8:25 to 8:45.",tip_b2:"When the news comes before the 9:30 open, the first 15-min candle after it is often wild. Waiting for it avoids entering on a false start.",tip_scen:"A scenario is an « if… then… » prepared before the open: the entry (where you get in), the stop (where you get out if you are wrong) and the target (where you take profit). The R compares what you aim for with what you risk: a 10-pt stop and a 40-pt target → 4R. At least 2R is needed. « Adjust » to change the prices.",tip_limits:"Your safeguards for the day. Max trades: past it, you stop. Time limit: no new trade after it. Max loss: if you hit it, your day is over. E.g. 2 trades, 11:30, $500.",tip_stopday:"What ends your day, even without a loss. E.g. your 2 scenarios are invalidated: the market is not doing what you planned, you close your platform.",tip_bias:"Your preferred direction for the day. Long: you mostly look for buys. Short: mostly for sells. Neutral: no view, you wait for price to choose.",tip_levels:"The prices you watch today, with their names. E.g. PDH 21,290 · London high 21,250 · London low 21,180.",tip_plan:"What you will do if the market goes the way of your bias, in one sentence. E.g. a break of the London high that holds on the retest: I buy toward the PDH.",tip_alt:"What you will do if the market goes the other way. E.g. back under the London low: I sell toward the PDL. Otherwise, no trade.",tip_maxloss:"The loss at which you stop for the day. Sweep starts from your account’s limit (or your drawdown room): never go above it.",title:"Pre-market",note:"Your note from last session",of:"{a} of {b}",next:"Continue",back:"Back",save:"Save my sheet",needs:"Fill in what is missing to continue.",base:"Today’s levels",instrument:"Instrument",inst_other:"Other",inst_ph:"Symbol, e.g. MNQ",inst_need:"Pick your instrument.",grp_lo